  "caveats": [
    "1. All 6 pre-registered Hamiltonians (M0-M5) have zero tunable or per-isotope parameters (CAL-1/2/3 only: proton-pinned q_0 and electron mass m_e in the documented E_osc(q_0) = m_e / (q_0 - 1)^2 and E_0(q_0) = m_e / (q_0(q_0 - 1)) charts). 2. Strong-sector models M0-M5 are strictly SU(2)_tau isospin-symmetric, so 3H and 3He receive identical strong binding before electromagnetic pp Coulomb + (m_n - m_p) core-breaking (~0.764 MeV empirical splitting). 3. Short-range (0s)^{3A} single-bag collapse is proved repulsive under O_CM (+56/3, +64, +128 for A=2,3,4), confirming that physical light-nuclei binding arises via virtual Bloch-Horowitz tunnelling from the factorized A-nucleon cluster channel into Pauli-conjugate [A,A,A] (x) [3^A] hidden-colour-spin-isospin channels rather than static 12-quark bag collapse."
  ],
